                        <h3 class="title">17. What is personal data?</h3>
                        <p class="f-18">
                            Personal data is information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person. An identifiable
                            natural person is one who can be identified, directly or indirectly, by reference to an identifier such as a
                            name, an identification number, location data, an online identifier or to one or more factors specific to
                            the physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity of that natural person.
                            We do not consider data that has been anonymised or aggregated so that it can no longer be used to
                            identify a specific natural person, whether in combination with other information or otherwise, as
                            personal data.
                            We collect personal data from you when you use our Services.
                        </p>

